  "schedule": "Sequential fresh workers, alternating baseline/cache order by round. Every worker verifies output SHA-256 and bytes, warms then measures three batches of requests. Warm cases reuse a connection; cold cases create a new connection before each request timer. Opening/closing connections excluded. Web Response body collection included for small cases; bulk controls use a counting Node writable. Natural GC. RSS is whole-worker high-water across verification, warmup and timed requests. Both versions use fixed 256-row batches, default 64 KiB output flush target, and memLevel 9 ZIP settings. No data or complete-response cache. This control caches table metadata/generated SQL but prepares fresh data statements for every export, removing statement leases. Query exports unchanged from the previous capability-only prototype."
